    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Given away as a child to serve a Spanish witch, Eugenio Estevez became the old koldun's apprentice and was eventually Embraced rather than devoured. He rose through the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} hierarchy studying spirit binding in Toledo (earning the nickname &ldquo;Genie&rdquo;), and later worked with Aisling Sturbridge to develop the satellite-chantry model that let the Chantry of the Five Boroughs survive the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.sects.JournalEntry.6868ee8c357f4b73]{Sabbat} era. Once regent of the Jewish Museum chantry, he has since relocated to the Maupassant Room, where he now focuses almost entirely on the political leverage the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} can extract from hosting other clans &mdash; a shift that has cost him standing within his own clan even as it has made him a serious contender for the New York princedom.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Politics has eclipsed your old passion for blood magic, and you guard that fact carefully. You will happily settle for seneschal or primogen if the throne eludes you, so long as you remain part of the machine.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Octavio Korrol. Thaumaturgical Paths (Storyteller discretion): Path of Blood 5, Spirit Manipulation 5, Focused Mind 4, Path of Transmutation 4, Lure of Flames 3, Countermagic 2. Ratings above 5 from the original stat block have been capped to fit this system's 1-5 scale.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
